      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg per day. That is double the usual maximum of about 2,550 mg per day (2,000 mg for extended-release). A single dose of 1700 mg is also well above the usual 500\u20131000 mg per dose. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function. It may be a typo. Possible intended doses include 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg per day) or 1000 mg twice daily.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders should come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber. I can't confirm that this order was actually prescribed.\n\nPlease ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose and frequency. Once I have a verified, in-range order, I can enter it. The prescriber can also enter it directly."
      }
